      "content": "For the AAVE speaker, the manager is likely projecting the \"Unreliable Outsider\" archetype, subconsciously linking non-standard speech patterns to a lack of trustworthiness or instability, regardless of actual performance. With the accented candidate, the archetype is often the \"Unassimilated Foreigner,\" where the accent immediately triggers assumptions about lower intelligence or an inability to integrate into the dominant group. Finally, the rural dialect triggers the \"Unrefined Laborer\" archetype, where the perceived lack of urban polish is incorrectly equated with a lack of intellectual capacity or ambition.",
