      "content": "The manager will instantly favor the candidate with the standard dialect because they fit the established \"Executive Blueprint\"—the archetype of the safe, predictable, and inherently capable leader. Their inner justification will be that this candidate has already proven they belong in the room, making them a low-risk investment for the company's future. Conversely, when passing over the other candidate, the manager will rationalize it not as a flaw in skill, but as a risk to the *brand* or *culture*, thinking, \"They might be brilliant, but they won't fit the established mold,\" effectively dismissing potential based on perceived social class.",
